WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.870
Speaker 1: We are starting to see a softening
in the pandemic recovery.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:08.010
And, yeah, some of it has to do with a..

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:13.610
Taxers, what has been a fantastic, you know,
80, 85, even 90 percent recovery from the

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.610
pandemic.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.160
And I mean, economically and I also mean from
a public health standpoint is now slowing

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.160
down.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.160
Now, you might be saying.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.939
Well, David, wait a second, are you criticizing
the state of play in the United States during

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:28.210
a Democratic administration?

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:33.370
I thought you were a Democratic shill or a
shill, as someone recently called me.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.579
No, you guys know, many of you know, I've
never been a Democrat.

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:39.030
I don't really care about the Democratic Party.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.649
I just call things the way they are.

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:45.640
And we are now seeing jobless claims up and
higher than expected.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:50.710
Initial jobless claims for the week ending
July 3rd came in at three hundred seventy

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.900
three thousand new jobless claims.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.829
That's higher than the three hundred and fifty
thousand that was expected.

00:00:56.829 --> 00:01:00.030
Initial unemployment claims had been on the
decline.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.820
Big picture for months now, but we're now
seeing a reversal.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.430
Jobless claims going up.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:10.910
Meanwhile, there are broader concerns about
the global economic comeback.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:16.840
Anecdotally, Japan has now declared a state
of emergency in Tokyo and covid cases are

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:17.979
surging globally.

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:23.060
They're surging in a number of countries and
overall and they're also up a bit, actually

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.180
close to 20 percent in the United States.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.650
Check out these numbers around the world.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:34.780
Cases had bottomed out in mid-June at about
three hundred and sixty thousand a day.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:41.101
Globally, cases are now up 12 percent just
in the last few weeks to over 400000 cases

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.140
a day.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:45.399
This is believed to be mostly because of the
more contagious Delta variant.

00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:50.000
These you know, sometimes people see something
on the news, more contagious Delta variant.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.260
That doesn't really mean anything.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:56.310
No, we are seeing because it spreads more
easily, 12 percent more cases globally per

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.310
day.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:01.420
There's now an even more contagious LAMDA
variant.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:06.030
We don't yet know much about it, which could
be the next to spread and become dominant.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:13.790
So cases up 12 percent globally in the United
States, cases are up 20 percent.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:16.900
We had gotten down to about 12000 cases a
day.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:18.520
In the US.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.560
We are now up to more than 14000 cases a day
in the U.S.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.950
That is a big jump.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.750
Now, so far, fortunately, we are not seeing
higher deaths.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.110
But remember that deaths lag cases by weeks.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:37.070
The hope would be the optimistic scenario
is even though we're seeing more cases because

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:42.900
Delta's more contagious, if you're vaccinated,
you still are unlikely to get hospitalized.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.820
If you get the virus and you're unlikely to
die if you get the virus if you are vaccinated.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.030
That's the hope.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.300
We don't really know that yet.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.650
We need another three to four weeks to see
if that's the case.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:58.190
And meanwhile, 20 percent of Americans still
don't want the vaccine if you care about public

00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:59.690
health.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:04.170
You would go and you would get the vaccine,
if you care about the economy, you would go

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.160
and you would get the vaccine.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:11.720
If you care about avoiding another sort of
shutdown to some degree in the fall, you would

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.220
go and you get the vaccine.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.420
What are we doing here?

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:19.810
Let's put up this pathetic chart of U.S. vaccinations
per day and you will see if you were watching

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:25.900
today that we are basically down to the level
of daily vaccination that we saw in January.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.460
Now, think back to that, OK?

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:31.940
In January, we had almost no vaccines.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.500
It was health care workers.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:38.360
And I think we were starting to make the vaccine
available to the oldest and most vulnerable.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.850
We are vaccinating the same amount of people
now.

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:44.390
When we have full availability, you just walk
in in many places.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.550
You don't even need an appointment.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:46.760
You just get vaccinated.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:52.350
And somehow we are vaccinating no more people
over the last week than we were doing in mid-January

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:58.030
when availability was close to not not literally
zero, but it was very, very low.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:03.880
And in other countries, people are just sitting
there waiting for the privilege of having

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.830
the vaccine access that we have.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:11.840
And we are seeing it reflected not just in
the case numbers, but in the economic uncertainty

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.840
as well.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:17.751
And so my appeal is, if you don't care about
other people, if you don't care, but if you

00:04:17.751 --> 00:04:21.850
just don't want to get vaccinated because
you have assessed that you were at low risk,

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:26.050
either accurately or not, and you don't really
care about other people or whatever else,

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:31.770
do you care about the economy because the
economy is wrapped up in the success of the

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.480
public health recovery?

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.690
Come on, guys.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:38.590
The world is desperate for the vaccines that
we have an overflow of.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.860
Just go and get vaccinated.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.060
Let me know your thoughts on this.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:48.580
Do you think that this will continue to worsen
or is this a temporary blip as we hopefully

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:51.450
get closer and closer to herd immunity?

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:52.450
Let me know.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.730
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman
and we will see.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.880
I mean, listen, but 10 days from now, we'll
have the answer.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.340
And hopefully it is a positive one and not
a negative one.

